<title>GREECE: GREEK DEALERS SEE AVG BID AT 99-99.50 FOR 3-YR BOND.</title>
<headline>GREEK DEALERS SEE AVG BID AT 99-99.50 FOR 3-YR BOND.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the results of an</p>
<p>informal Reuters poll of dealers on the average accepted bid of</p>
<p>three-, five- and seven-year coupon bonds auctioned today by the</p>
<p>finance ministry.</p>
<p>Dealers were asked to predict the average accepted bid that</p>
<p>today's auction of three-, five- and seven-year paper will</p>
<p>produce.</p>
<p>				RANGE OF AVG ACCEPTED BIDS</p>
<p>  3-YEAR COUPON BOND:	 99-99.50</p>
<p>  5-YEAR COUPON BOND:	 97.90-99</p>
<p>  7-YEAR COUPON BOND:	 95.95-99</p>
<p>The range of forecasts was wider for Greece's five-and</p>
<p>seven-year bonds auctioned for the first time ever.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
